From: =?UTF-8?q?Tobias=20Frauenschl=C3=A4ger?= <t.frauenschlaeger@me.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:22:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] drivers: clock_control: mcux_syscon: fix RW6xx ENET clock
 rate
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On RW6xx, MCUX_ENET_CLK reported CLOCK_GetTddrMciEnetClkFreq(), the
fixed 50 MHz TDDR ENET clock that serves as the PTP time base. The
ENET MAC and MDIO drivers use this rate to compute the MDC divider,
but the ENET module runs from the main clock (260 MHz). MDC therefore
ran at about 13 MHz, above the 10 MHz MDIO limit of PHYs such as the
KSZ8081, and the PHY never answered.

Report the main clock instead, which is what the MCUXpresso SDK ENET
examples pass to ENET_SetSMI(). The PTP clock uses the separate
MCUX_ENET_PLL subsystem and is not affected.

Signed-off-by: Tobias Frauenschläger <t.frauenschlaeger@me.com>
---
 drivers/clock_control/clock_control_mcux_syscon.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clock_control/clock_control_mcux_syscon.c b/drivers/clock_control/clock_control_mcux_syscon.c
index f14aedf6c02..febd895d77d 100644
--- a/drivers/clock_control/clock_control_mcux_syscon.c
+++ b/drivers/clock_control/clock_control_mcux_syscon.c
@@ -512,7 +512,7 @@ static int mcux_lpc_syscon_clock_control_get_subsys_rate(const struct device *de
 #ifdef CONFIG_ETH_NXP_ENET
 	case MCUX_ENET_CLK:
 #ifdef CONFIG_SOC_SERIES_RW6XX
-		*rate = CLOCK_GetTddrMciEnetClkFreq();
+		*rate = CLOCK_GetMainClkFreq();
 #endif
 		break;
 #endif
